<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tamaulipas</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tamaulipas is a state of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>, bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande">Rio Grande</a>, with Ciudad Victoria as its capital. Colonised from 1748 as the Spanish province of Nuevo Santander, it became a state of independent Mexico in 1824. Its southern part lies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huasteca">Huasteca</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tamaulipas.jpg" alt="Tamaulipas" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: panza.rayada · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Bernalito,_en_el_valle_abajo_de_la_Cuesta_de_Llera_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
